hase; some card or enemy effects can also end your turn.\nEnergy A/B means A energy available now and B normal energy recharge per turn; B is not a cap. At the start of your turn, energy resets to B, except Ice Cream retains unused energy and adds B; other effects can add energy. Ordinary Block is removed at the start of your turn; Barricade or Blur preserves it, otherwise Calipers removes 15 instead. Unless an effect retains them, remaining hand cards are discarded at end of turn (Ethereal cards Exhaust); you normally draw the displayed draw-per-turn amount for the next turn. Listed player powers omit zero values: absent Strength or Dexterity means zero. A shown intent describes the upcoming enemy phase.\nCard rules below describe the named instance: + means upgraded. Rule damage/Block are unmodified unless explicitly calculated; inline deal N already includes current attack modifiers. Battle turns start at 0.\nCurrent direct Block calculation for Defend: 5 (includes current Dexterity, Frail and No Block; excludes other card-play triggers, copies and later changes).\n\n\n\n-- KEY (effects/statuses; numbers are shown next to each above) --\n  Frail: the affected creature gains 25% less Block from cards; its number is turns remaining.\n  Vulnerable: the affected creature takes 50% more damage from attacks (already reflected in the shown deal N); its number is turns remaining.\n  Bash: Deal 8 damage. Apply 2 Vulnerable.\n  Strike: Deal 6 damage.\n  Forethought: Put a card from your hand on the bottom of your draw pile; it costs 0 until played.\n  Defend: Gain 5 Block.\n  Slimed: Status. Costs 1 to play; Exhaust. Does nothing else.\n  Jack of All Trades: Add 1 random colorless cards to your hand. Exhaust.\n  Burning Blood: At the end of combat, heal 6 HP.",
